  "amendment_date": "2026-10-26",
  "amendment": "Preserve current main behavior (98e64a6 at this merge), including independent per-key completions, immediate CEC admission while ACKs are pending, wait_for_release and fixed Siri macros. Distribution only moves messages to their owner and has zero CEC behavioral effect; d50af8026938797fc0820d0107f4c4e064c2d2bc remains historical evidence where unchanged. State-change-only transport; executor owns button/message choices and successful completion pacing, has no TX buffer and supplies one attempt per key press. Failed key TX ends that key state; later up is a no-op. Global release is implicit at recipient stream end only when all its keys cease being pressed, including last-key failure. CEC mechanically sends supplied frames through eight total messages per wire; releases at eight are dropped without executor admission retry, and every TX dropped because the FIFO is full is logged. Necessary bounded task communication queues remain permitted, not outgoing/retry backlogs. Prior original-controller/headless, baseline-UI, hostname, settings, removal-reset and manual-recovery amendments remain in force. The 26 October 2026 hardware amendment limits each Amity to four tentacles/eight CEC ports, retains the one-tentacle default on GPIO1/2, and gives the optional four-slot XIAO profile overridable GPIO pairs 1/2, 5/6, 7/8 and 9/44.",
